statement:
Assume (TL): for all P, n ∈ ℕ, every open U ⊆ ℝ^P and all Borel sets A ⊆ B ⊆ U with Hⁿ(B ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U (Hⁿ = μHE[n]), for Hⁿ-a.e. x ∈ A and every linear subspace Q of ℝ^P: B has approximate tangent space Q at x iff A has approximate tangent space Q at x (HasApproximateTangentSpaceAt, Simon Ch. 3, 1.4).
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P open, M ⊆ U Borel and countably (n+1)-rectifiable with H^{n+1}(M ∩ K) < ∞ for every compact K ⊆ U, and f : ℝ^P → ℝ L-Lipschitz (L ≥ 0). Then there exist, for j ∈ ℕ, sets V_j, C_j, Y_j ⊆ ℝ^{n+1}, maps ψ_j : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P and F_j : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ, and a map g : ℝ^P → ℝ^P such that:
(a) V_j is open, ψ_j is C¹ on V_j and injective on V_j, Dψ_j(y) is injective for every y ∈ V_j, and ψ_j(V_j) ⊆ U;
(b) C_j is compact, C_j ⊆ V_j, Y_j is Borel, Y_j ⊆ C_j, and F_j is C¹ on ℝ^{n+1};
(c) ψ_j(Y_j) ⊆ M for every j, the sets ψ_j(Y_j) are pairwise disjoint, and H^{n+1}(M ∖ ⋃_j ψ_j(Y_j)) = 0;
(d) for every j and y ∈ Y_j: f(ψ_j(y)) = F_j(y), and M has approximate tangent space Dψ_j(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) at ψ_j(y) (dimension n+1);
(e) g is Borel, |g(x)| ≤ L for every x, g(x) = 0 whenever x ∉ ⋃_j ψ_j(Y_j), and for every j and y ∈ Y_j: g(ψ_j(y)) ∈ Dψ_j(y)(ℝ^{n+1}) and ⟨g(ψ_j(y)), Dψ_j(y)e⟩ = DF_j(y)e for every e ∈ ℝ^{n+1}.
(g is the tangential gradient ∇^M f of Simon Ch. 3, 2.1, on the pieces ψ_j(Y_j).)
